Have you every felt Imposter Syndrome yourself and, if you’re comfortable sharing, how did it manifest itself? What, if anything, has helped you mitigate these feelings?
Yes, I have. It usually shows up as procrastination, avoidance, and fear of starting something new.
What helps me is taking time to "recharge" — once I regain energy, I feel more capable of overcoming obstacles again.
What do you think are some of the immediate or long-term effects of Imposter Syndrome if left unchecked?
It can lead to giving up. If you don’t address it, you might stop pursuing the things you really want to do.
